-- title:
--   Bounded rigidification exponent on an edge chart
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $r$ and a complete discrete valuation ring $\mathcal O$ of characteristic zero which is a domain, with irreducible element $\pi$, residue ring of cardinality $r$, and $(r)=(\pi)$, together with a fraction field $K_0$ of $\mathcal O$ of characteristic zero; let $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra which is a domain of characteristic zero in which the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$ is maximal. Let $\iota$ be a ring homomorphism from $\mathbb{Z}_{r^2}$, realised as the Witt vectors of $\mathrm{GF}(r^2)$, into $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$, and let $\Phi$ be a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/rO^{\mathrm{nr}}$ that is special for the reduction of $\iota$ (its Lie algebra splits as the direct sum of the two invertible eigen-submodules for the action twisted by $\iota$ and by its Frobenius twist) and has height $4$. Let `MD` be a moduli package over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ satisfying the Zariski sheaf condition, and let $\eta$ assign, to each commutative ring $B$, each ring homomorphism $\psi : O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to B$ with $r$ nilpotent in $B$, and each rigidified datum $t=(X,n,\rho)$ over $B$ (a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X$ over $B$, a natural number $n$, and a $2$-tuple of power series $\rho$ over $B/rB$), a point of `MD.obj B ψ`. The hypothesis `hη` is the conjunction of three conditions over Noetherian test rings: $\eta$ separates admissible data exactly up to the isomorphism relation for rigidified data; $\eta$ commutes with base change along ring homomorphisms compatible with the structure morphisms, applied to admissible data; and every point of `MD.obj B ψ` is, Zariski-locally on $\operatorname{Spec} B$ (along a finite family generating the unit ideal, with localisations away from its members), the image under $\eta$ of an admissible datum. Here admissibility of $t$ for $(\iota,\psi)$ means that $X$ is special for $\psi\circ\iota$, that $X$ has height $4$, and that $\rho$ is an isogeny of height $4n$ from the base change of $\Phi$ to the reduction of $X$. Finally, let $e$ be a family of maps, indexed by the Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebras $B$ in which the image of $\pi$ is nilpotent, from the points of `ModuliPackage.G 𝒪 MD` over $B$ — triples consisting of an $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism $\psi : O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to B$, nilpotence of $r$ in $B$, and a point of `MD.obj B ψ` — to the product of the functor corepresented by $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ with Deligne's functor $\Omega$ for $(K_0,\pi)$, assumed natural in $B$, bijective for every such $B$, and such that its first component is the coefficient homomorphism $\psi$. The conclusion: for every pair of full $\mathcal O$-lattices $M' \subseteq M$ in $K_0^2$ with $\pi M \subseteq M'$ there is a natural number $N_\gamma$ such that for every local Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with the image of $\pi$ nilpotent and every point $y$ over $B$, if the Deligne datum $e(y)_2$ lies in the edge chart of $(M',M)$ — that is, at every prime $\mathfrak p$ of $B$ one has $M'\subseteq M$, $\pi M \subseteq M'$, no $v \in M \setminus M'$ has $1 \otimes v$ in the line at $M$ plus $\mathfrak p$ times the whole base change, and no $v' \in M'$ outside $\pi M$ has $1 \otimes v'$ in the line at $M'$ plus $\mathfrak p$ times the whole base change — then there is a rigidified datum $t$ over $B$, admissible for $(\iota, y.\psi)$, with $\eta$ of $t$ equal to the moduli point of $y$ and with $t.n \le N_\gamma$.
--
--   This is the bounded-exponent statement for the Čerednik–Drinfeld comparison: over a single edge chart of Drinfeld's formal upper half plane, the points of the moduli functor are represented by admissible rigidified formal $\mathcal O_D$-modules whose rigidification exponent is bounded by a constant depending only on the edge $(M',M)$, uniformly over all local Noetherian test algebras. It feeds the existence and uniqueness of even rigidified pairs and the open-immersion property of the stratum windows in the fake elliptic curve theory.
